From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: SDR color management through the DPU output LUTs

Without per-plane color management gamescope only applies its color
pipeline in the composite shader, so a directly scanned-out layer loses
night mode and the color sliders. The msm DPU's post-blend CRTC
DEGAMMA_LUT (256) and 17^3 DPU_3D_LUT are the same shape as the shader's
shaper and 3D LUT, so an SDR gamma 2.2 output can carry that chain in
hardware. Enabling them changes which display blocks the CRTC owns, so
that transition needs a modeset; being post-blend, a translucent overlay
is corrected as the blended pixel. Per-plane offload is the follow-up.
---
